(Agent Hijack Shield: Setup on Another Windows Laptop) Tj
T*
T*
(This guide installs the local demo on a second Windows 10/11 computer and connects its) Tj
T*
(Chrome extension to that computer's local backend. GitHub carries the source code; the) Tj
T*
(backend, policy database, and browser extension must each be set up on the laptop where) Tj
T*
(ChatGPT will be used.) Tj
T*
T*
(What you need) Tj
T*
T*
(  - Windows 10 or 11) Tj
T*
(  - Git for Windows) Tj
T*
(  - Python 3.11 or newer) Tj
T*
(  - Google Chrome) Tj
T*
(  - Internet access for cloning and installing Python packages) Tj
T*
T*
(This prototype covers ChatGPT in Chrome only. It does not monitor the ChatGPT desktop) Tj
T*
(app, other browsers, PDFs, Office documents, pasted text, or drag-and-drop uploads.) Tj
T*
T*
(  * Get the project) Tj
T*
T*
(Install Git for Windows and Python 3.11+ if they are not already installed. During) Tj
T*
(Python setup, enable **Add Python to PATH**.) Tj
T*
T*
(Open PowerShell and run:) Tj
T*
T*
(    git clone https://github.com/jagatheip74-hub/agent-hijack-shield-2.git) Tj
T*
(    Set-Location agent-hijack-shield-2) Tj
T*
T*
(  * Set up the local backend) Tj
T*
T*
(From the project root in PowerShell:) Tj
T*
T*
(    py -3 -m venv backend\\.venv) Tj
T*
(    .\\backend\\.venv\\Scripts\\Activate.ps1) Tj
T*
(    python -m pip install --upgrade pip) Tj
T*
(    python -m pip install -r backend\\requirements.txt) Tj
T*
T*
(If PowerShell blocks environment activation, run this in the same window and activate) Tj
T*
(again:) Tj
T*
T*
(    Set-ExecutionPolicy -Scope Process -ExecutionPolicy Bypass) Tj
T*
(    .\\backend\\.venv\\Scripts\\Activate.ps1) Tj
T*
T*
(  * Install the Chrome extension and copy its ID) Tj
T*
T*
(  * Open Chrome and enter chrome://extensions in the address bar.) Tj
T*
(  * Turn on **Developer mode**.) Tj
T*
(  * Click **Load unpacked**.) Tj
T*
(  * Choose the browser-extension folder inside the cloned project. For example:) Tj
T*
ET
endstream
