T*
(Supported files and important limits) Tj
T*
T*
(  - Supported extensions: .txt, .md, .csv, .json.) Tj
T*
(  - Maximum five files per selection.) Tj
T*
(  - Each file must be at most 48 KiB and contain 1 to 12,000 characters.) Tj
T*
(  - The extension scans the file text locally before releasing a supported file-picker) Tj
T*
(selection to ChatGPT.) Tj
T*
(  - The scanner uses heuristics. It can miss suspicious content and can flag harmless) Tj
T*
(content.) Tj
T*
(  - This prototype does not cover PDFs, Office files, pasted content, drag-and-drop,) Tj
T*
(other AI apps, the ChatGPT desktop app, or every alternate upload path. It is not) Tj
T*
(production-grade endpoint security.) Tj
T*
(  - Do not upload confidential, personal, or secret data while testing. A file approved) Tj
T*
(by this local scanner is then sent to ChatGPT by the browser.) Tj
T*
T*
(Troubleshooting) Tj
T*
T*
(**Upload reports a connection or fetch error:** Make sure the backend PowerShell window) Tj
T*
(is still running. Check that CORS_ORIGINS includes the exact chrome-extension:// ID from) Tj
T*
(this laptop, then restart the backend after changing it.) Tj
T*
T*
(**Every upload is blocked for lack of policy:** Run the policy command once and confirm) Tj
T*
(it returns the Allow ChatGPT text uploads policy.) Tj
T*
T*
(**The safe test file is blocked as unsupported or too large:** Use a .txt, .md, .csv, or) Tj
T*
(.json file under 48 KiB and 12,000 characters.) Tj
T*
T*
(**The extension does not appear on ChatGPT:** Confirm it is enabled at) Tj
T*
(chrome://extensions, open https://chatgpt.com in the same Chrome profile, and reload the) Tj
T*
(page.) Tj
T*
T*
(**After restarting Windows:** Start the backend again using step 4 before uploading. The) Tj
T*
(backend is a local process and does not start automatically.) Tj
T*
ET
